      "statement": "SFUTopology routes all P2P traffic through a single SFU peer (the numerically lowest peer ID by default, or an explicitly set one — peer IDs are sequential decimal strings, so election sorts parseInt(id, 10) rather than lexicographically); the SFU offers to every client and non-SFU peers connect only to the SFU, trading a single point of failure for better large-group scalability.",
