    {
      "id": "claim_94dec8e87c65413b9d94fa60a17902c9",
      "statement": "On a hubInfoMessage the client reconciles its local peer roster against the authoritative roster carried in the message: it adds any roster peer not yet in the map and prunes any peer it still holds that is no longer listed and is not itself, firing ZeroHubDisconnected and tearing the peer down via the shared removePeer helper. This prune pass is the auto-reconnect fix; without it a peer that left the hub while the socket was down would linger as a stale Peer holding a live, unclosed RTCPeerConnection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://client/src/zeroHub.ts#L405-L453",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c5329aa7d7171db5bbf5441d6784f1102fe52869b66705185ed0966b8360d4a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f2fc909679c64c51b575825c7dc469b9",
      "statement": "Hub and peer metadata received from the server is parsed through the module-level safeParseJson(raw, fallback) helper, which returns the parsed JSON on success or the fallback when the input is missing or malformed; the caller logs a warning only on a genuine parse failure, so a corrupt metadata value from the server degrades to the fallback instead of throwing and crashing the WebSocket message dispatcher.",
      "evidence": [
